{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794363830994,"sessionID":"ses_e37c0206bffe1WqCsLDh8xik5o","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_194feca3f6d340038633acfa","state":{"status":"error","input":{"command":"setsid gunicorn --bind 127.0.0.1:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app --workers 1 < /dev/null > .server.log 2>&1 & sleep 3; curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/health; echo; TOK=$(curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/register -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"username\":\"demo\",\"password\":\"secret123\"}' -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}'); echo \"register -> $TOK\"; TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/auth/login -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"username\":\"demo\",\"password\":\"secret123\"}' | python3 -c 'import sys,json;print(json.load(sys.stdin)[\"token\"])'); echo \"login ok, token ${TOKEN:0:8}…\"; curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/entries -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"project\":\"Alpha\",\"description\":\"Setup environment\",\"hours\":2.5,\"date\":\"2026-11-10\"}' | python3 -m json.tool; curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/entries | python3 -c 'import sys,json;d=json.load(sys.stdin);print(\"list total:\",d[\"total\"],\"first:\",d[\"items\"][0][\"project\"],d[\"items\"][0][\"hours\"])'; curl -s -D - -o /tmp/opencode/e.csv -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/exports/entries.csv | grep -i 'content-type\\|content-disposition'; cat /tmp/opencode/e.csv; curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"GET / -> %{http_code}\\n\" http://127.0.0.1:8000/","workdir":"/workspace"},"error":"The user has specified a rule which prevents you from using this specific tool call. Here are some of the relevant rules [{\"permission\":\"*\",\"action\":\"allow\",\"pattern\":\"*\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"*\",\"action\":\"ask\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"/run/home/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/*\",\"action\":\"allow\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"/tmp/opencode/*\",\"action\":\"allow\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"action\":\"deny\",\"pattern\":\"*\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"/run/home/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/*\",\"action\":\"allow\"}]","time":{"start":1794363830980,"end":1794363830990}},"id":"prt_1c86b32bb001PLPmE7ErGXBONM","sessionID":"ses_e37c0206bffe1WqCsLDh8xik5o","messageID":"msg_1c86ad84d001LBIrneOjFt0D35"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794363831016,"sessionID":"ses_e37c0206bffe1WqCsLDh8xik5o","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_7bbc2f487ac347248a559173","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/README.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # App\n2: \n3: ## Run contract\n4: \n5: - The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n6: - The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n7: - The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n8: - Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n9: \n10: ## Layout\n11: \n12: - `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n13: - `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n14: \n15: Dependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).\n\n(End of file - total 15 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# App\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/README.md","text":"# App\n\n## Run contract\n\n- The app is built from `Dockerfile` in this directory and the container listens on port 8000.\n- The API is served under `/api`. `GET /api/health` answers `{\"status\": \"ok\"}` once the app is ready.\n- The backend also serves the frontend build at `/`.\n- Persistent data lives in `./data` (relative to the working directory `/app`).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `backend/`: the Flask app (`backend/app.py`, served by gunicorn as `app:app`); dependencies in `backend/requirements.txt`.\n- `frontend/`: a Vite project (React + TypeScript). `npm run build` writes `frontend/dist`, which the image copies next to the backend.\n\nDependencies are pinned: `backend/requirements.lock` holds the resolved versions and is installed as a pip constraints file. The frontend uses `frontend/package-lock.json` (`npm ci`). When you change dependencies, update the lock file as well (or remove it).","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":15,"totalLines":15,"truncated":false}},"title":"README.md","time":{"start":1794363830968,"end":1794363830996}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c86b32b2001nUvXz5VowuTrGe","sessionID":"ses_e37c0206bffe1WqCsLDh8xik5o","messageID":"msg_1c86ad84d001LBIrneOjFt0D35"}}
